  "verbalization": "CID 442993 is linked to Hepatocyte, which is the target of both (2E)-2-[(5S,6R,10S)-10-hydroxy-6-(3-hydroxypropyl)-4-methoxy-10-methyl-3-[(3Z,5E)-11-methyl-7-methylidenedodeca-3,5,10-trien-3-yl]spiro[4.5]decan-7-ylidene]propanal and Licochalcone D. Both of these compounds are known to target Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, suggesting a shared mechanism of action. The evidence points to a potential pathway where CID 442993 may interact with Hepatocyte through these compounds, which in turn inhibit Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on these compounds to modulate the activity of the phosphatase, potentially through a common target or a shared regulatory mechanism. The evidence supports a relationship where CID 442993 may influence the activity of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP via its interaction with Hepatocyte and the subsequent targeting of this phosphatase by related compounds.",
